  "question": {
    "text": "Let the straight line $\\mathrm{y}=2 \\mathrm{x}$ touch a circle with center $(0, \\alpha), \\alpha>0$, and radius $\\mathrm{r}$ at a point $\\mathrm{A}_1$. Let $\\mathrm{B}_1$ be the point on the circle such that the line segment $A_1 B_1$ is a diameter of the circle. Let $\\alpha+r=5+\\sqrt{5}$.\nMatch each entry in List-I to the correct entry in List-II.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/nWsazjEVEIvd2DADB_ki9u2SVxCfJacnU4_SczRNUoA.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nThe correct option is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3Ckn7",
      "text": "$(\\mathrm{P}) \\rightarrow(4) \\quad(\\mathrm{Q}) \\rightarrow(2) \\quad(\\mathrm{R}) \\rightarrow(1) \\quad(\\mathrm{S}) \\rightarrow(3)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FCisF",
      "text": "$(\\mathrm{P}) \\rightarrow(2) \\quad(\\mathrm{Q}) \\rightarrow(4) \\quad(\\mathrm{R}) \\rightarrow(1) \\quad(\\mathrm{S}) \\rightarrow(3)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jrk5E",
      "text": "$(\\mathrm{P}) \\rightarrow(4) \\quad(\\mathrm{Q}) \\rightarrow(2) \\quad(\\mathrm{R}) \\rightarrow(5) \\quad(\\mathrm{S}) \\rightarrow(3)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HNVDc",
      "text": "$(\\mathrm{P}) \\rightarrow(2) \\quad(\\mathrm{Q}) \\rightarrow(4) \\quad(\\mathrm{R}) \\rightarrow(3) \\quad(\\mathrm{S}) \\rightarrow(5)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/vjzEO8CmfhM_MGYXOYShuN-ACF1qdKCwP0v23RKfFIY.original.fullsize.png\">\nConsider centre as $\\mathrm{P}(0, \\alpha), \\alpha>0$\n$\\left|\\frac{2(0)-\\alpha}{\\sqrt{5}}\\right|=r$\n$\\begin{aligned}& |-\\alpha|=\\sqrt{5} r \\\\& \\alpha=\\sqrt{5} r \\\\& \\therefore \\alpha+r=5+\\sqrt{5} \\\\& \\sqrt{5} r+r=\\sqrt{5}(\\sqrt{5}+1) \\\\& r=\\sqrt{5}, \\alpha=5 \\\\& \\therefore P(0,5)\\end{aligned}$\nFoot of perpendicular from $\\mathrm{P}$ to line $2 \\mathrm{x}-\\mathrm{y}=0$\n$\\begin{aligned}& \\frac{x-0}{2}=\\frac{y-5}{-1}=\\frac{-(2(0)-5)}{5}=1 \\\\& x=2, y=4 \\quad A_1(2,4)\\end{aligned}$\nLet $\\mathrm{B}(\\mathrm{p}, \\mathrm{q})$\r\n$\\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{p}+2}{2}=0, \\frac{\\mathrm{q}+4}{2}=5$\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{p}=-2, \\mathrm{q}=6 \\quad \\mathrm{~B}(-2,6)$",
    "image": null
  },
